WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.540
Last week, I did a video about pedestrian crossings,

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:07.720
and while I don't want this to turn into 'things you might not know about British pedestrian crossings,'

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.500
Well, there is one more thing, and quite a few people got in touch to say I should point it out.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:18.420
There is a secret button, or nodule, on the bottom of these things you push when you want to cross the road.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.840
And what that little secret nodule is, is a sign for anyone who is blind and deaf,

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.220
or partially blind and partially deaf.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.820
Or, who is partially blind and at a crossing that does not make a beeping noise when it's safe to cross,

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.940
which is a surprising amount of crossings.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:37.980
Because that little nodule rotates any time that signal turns green, as we will now see.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.840
Because don't forget, disability isn't a thing that turns on or off,

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:50.060
you don't just get people who are entirely blind but fine every other way, or entirely deaf but perfectly able to see.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:55.700
You get lots of folks who might be able to walk around safely in the world, but who couldn't make out that signal,

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:00.040
and who couldn't work out the beeping from the background noise, even if there was some.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.240
So that little nodule means it's safe for a lot of British people to cross the road,

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.440
and that is something you might not have

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.440
[laughing over the sound of a bus]

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.440
Why do I do videos near roads?

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.320
THAT is something you might not have known!

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.020
[Translating these subtitles? Add your name here!]

